{"version":"0.12.27","prev_tag":"v0.12.26","target":"default","tag_prefix":"","area_scope":[],"commits":[{"sha":"1f5f0c4e45c79ca45cd1b6f4c0cdf7427ae9f12e","title":"resource-recovery: bound busy uv cache cleanup (#1358)","files":["TESTING.md","python/tests/test_resource_envelope.py","scripts/resource_envelope.py"]},{"sha":"00cf9dffe840d0c96c579667b8da22dfa03939bc","title":"pr-publication-continuity: retain Task PR identity through failures (#1359)","files":["rust/loopflow/src/ops/pr.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/pr_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_pr_authority_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_pr_range_tests.rs"]},{"sha":"3dc89bc9a062148a884e36db8f9528842e833d13","title":"Remove the resident Wave service and chat surfaces (#1360)","files":[".github/workflows/package-build.yml","README.md","TESTING.md","docs/agent-api.md","docs/architecture-reference.md","docs/architecture.html","docs/architecture.md","docs/architecture/codebase.md","docs/architecture/delivery.md","docs/architecture/homes.md","docs/architecture/planning.md","docs/conducting.md","docs/getting-started.md","docs/index.md","docs/lf-reference.md","docs/security.md","docs/troubleshooting.md","docs/waves.md","python/tests/test_architecture.py","python/tests/test_install_script.py","python/tests/test_loopflow_skill_alignment.py","python/tests/test_release_automation.py","python/tests/test_release_loopflow.py","python/tests/test_release_publisher.py","python/tests/test_shell_installer.py","release/install.sh","rust/loopflow/Cargo.toml","rust/loopflow/benches/wave_stream.rs","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lfd.rs","rust/loopflow/src/chat/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/chat/turns.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/README.md","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/channel.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/chat.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/chat_reply.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/discord.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/journal.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/placement.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/playhead.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/recovery.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/registry.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/relocate.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/resident.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/runner.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/runtime.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/server.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/state.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/subscription.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/supervisor.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/wave/wire.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/init.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/loopflow.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/wave_chat.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/process.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/wave_home.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/chat.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/doctor.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/fixtures.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/home.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install/published.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install/recovery.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/reply.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ssh.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/thread.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/util.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/waves.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lfd/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lfd/service.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lib.rs","rust/loopflow/src/machine_install.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/home.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pr_landing.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_destination.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/children.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/provider_deliveries.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/provider_deliveries.rs","rust/loopflow/src/wave_host.rs","rust/loopflow/src/webhook.rs","rust/loopflow/src/work/wave/config.rs","rust/loopflow/src/work/wave/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/context_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/global_commands.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/lfd_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/linear_webhook_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/support/installation.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_initialization_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/wave_journal_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/wave_live_smoke.rs"]},{"sha":"4a696c074073ab78b3cc0963af89b75ed7192204","title":"Defer the hosted CI matrix until PR scratch is clear (#1361)","files":[".github/workflows/ci.yml","TESTING.md","docs/architecture/delivery.md","python/tests/test_ci_proof.py"]},{"sha":"da31960c790f400bd7e685b5f51479f52429193c","title":"Bound agent launch context and keep progress out of Task steering (#1362)","files":["docs/agent-api.md","docs/lf-reference.md","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/LOOPFLOW.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/context_budget.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/launch.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/prompt.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/child.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/linear_observe.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/task_comments_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/src/run_record.rs","tests/goldens/basic.md","tests/goldens/builtin_debug.md","tests/goldens/builtin_implement.md","tests/goldens/builtin_realign.md","tests/goldens/with_docs.md"]},{"sha":"458fa141d2e6347c636441389d3896d941dcb839","title":"Prevent failed searches from falsely blocking Task handoff (#1363)","files":["docs/security.md","rust/loopflow/src/controller/task/mod.rs"]},{"sha":"e744f70690384f305755cadc638b8d14b6080d0e","title":"Prioritize planned deletions before implementation and polishing (#1364)","files":["rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/compress.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/design.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/implement.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/kickoff.md","tests/goldens/builtin_implement.md"]},{"sha":"e14a1d03518672794aa1615b9584cd54866ae20b","title":"Refresh account status and preserve account choices across Flow resumes (#1365)","files":["docs/getting-started.md","docs/subscriptions.md","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/init.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/loopflow.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/invocation.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/auth.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/auth_status.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/util.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/flow_run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/flow_session.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/human_session.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_destination.rs","rust/loopflow/src/provider_account.rs","rust/loopflow/src/provider_account/identity.rs","rust/loopflow/src/provider_account/lease.rs","rust/loopflow/src/provider_auth/codex.rs","rust/loopflow/src/provider_auth/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations/drafts/provider_account_credential_identity__53abefb58baad3a0448cee3babc1edb4.sql","rust/loopflow/src/store/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite.rs","rust/loopflow/src/subscription.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/agent_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/auth_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/flow_tests.rs","tests/fixtures/dto/auth_status.json"]},{"sha":"31c6e5d8fb3ff4f339715e3f46acca116c406d9e","title":"Keep saved plans from activating unrelated skills (#1366)","files":["PROMPTS.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/design.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/implement.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/kickoff.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/prompt.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/realign.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/review-design.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/launch.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/prompt.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","tests/goldens/builtin_implement.md","tests/goldens/builtin_realign.md","tests/goldens/with_docs.md"]},{"sha":"e88c34a674fed2f94b24964606fbcdfb91b760ec","title":"Merge Task branch updates without rewriting authored history (#1367)","files":["PROMPTS.md","README.md","TESTING.md","docs/agent-api.md","docs/architecture-reference.md","docs/architecture/codebase.md","docs/architecture/data.md","docs/architecture/delivery.md","docs/authoring.md","docs/config.md","docs/glossary.md","docs/lf-reference.md","docs/lf.md","docs/troubleshooting.md","python/tests/test_checkout_refresh.py","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/controller/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/LOOPFLOW.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/pr-land.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/pr-submit.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/rebase-conflicts.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/sync-conflicts.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/project/skill/testing-audit.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/flow/refresh.yaml","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/ci-fix.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/launch-plan.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/prompt.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/ship-decomposed.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow_graph.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/git.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/checkout.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/error.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/git_operation.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/land.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pr.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pr_landing.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/rebase.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/release.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/sync.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_actions.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/telemetry.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/children.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/children.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/git_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/global_commands.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/land_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/rebase_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/sync_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_initialization_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_pr_authority_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/task_pr_range_tests.rs","scripts/test.py","skills/loopflow/SKILL.md","tests/e2e/test_rebase_safety.sh","tests/e2e/test_sync_safety.sh","tests/goldens/basic.md","tests/goldens/builtin_debug.md","tests/goldens/builtin_implement.md","tests/goldens/builtin_realign.md","tests/goldens/with_docs.md"]}],"merged_prs":[{"number":1358,"title":"resource-recovery: bound busy uv cache cleanup","body":"Busy uv cache pruning can stall resource recovery while an enclosing uv process holds the cache lock. Bound pruning to 15 seconds, retain the busy cache, and continue cleanup of eligible build artifacts.\n\nExtracted independently from #1296; its execution-model work remains there.\n\nValidation: all 12 resource-envelope tests pass, including real temporary uv locks and build cleanup; Ruff and diff checks pass.\n","files":[],"additions":106,"deletions":45,"changed_files":3,"merge_commit":"1f5f0c4e45c79ca45cd1b6f4c0cdf7427ae9f12e"},{"number":1359,"title":"pr-publication-continuity: retain Task PR identity through failures","body":"A successful GitHub PR creation or discovery could lose its Task association when the next read or draft promotion failed. Persist the acknowledged PR identity before those operations, adopt existing PRs without requiring prior local publication, and retain reviewer copy until promotion succeeds. Linear linkage remains retryable after identity is saved. Recheck the publication base under the existing mutation lock.\n\nExtracted from #1296 without its execution-model or schema changes.\n\nValidation: all 50 runnable tests in pr_tests, task_pr_authority_tests and task_pr_range_tests pass with no fail-fast (one skipped). All-target Clippy with warnings denied, formatting and diff checks pass. Tests use isolated Homes, local Git and simulated GitHub effects.\n","files":[],"additions":339,"deletions":55,"changed_files":5,"merge_commit":"00cf9dffe840d0c96c579667b8da22dfa03939bc"},{"number":1360,"title":"Remove the resident Wave service and chat surfaces","body":"Remove the resident Wave service so Wave planning and Task delivery can ship without maintaining the listener, resident, daemon, or chat stack. Jack Heart requested the largest straightforward functionality cut from [LOO-298 · PR #1296](https://github.com/loopflowstudio/loopflow/pull/1296) that can land independently of its new execution model.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Delete the listener/resident runtime, `lfd`, Wave chat/reply/thread surfaces, webhook receiver and provider-delivery code.\n- Remove Swift chat views, streaming clients, resident liveness controls, their fixtures, tests and benchmarks.\n- Remove daemon packaging and installation requirements; keep PR landing on its existing foreground supervisor.\n- Update the CLI and architecture documentation. Bounded `lf --wave <name> wave/operate`, Tasks, chapters and metrics remain available.\n\nThe cut takes deletions and call-site hunks from `a0c919803` and removes newly orphaned private helpers. Against v0.12.26, the result is 421 lines added and 35,333 removed across 159 files. No database table or migration changed.\n\n## Left for #1296\n\nMain still needs `controller/wave/metrics.rs`, Wave-row registration, relocation at its existing module path, and the short-ID formatter used by Runs and usage. Its Task/Flow/chapter/Run model is unchanged. Historical daemon artifact identities remain readable in installation receipts; no daemon starts. Wave chat configuration vocabulary remains in goal parsing, without a bridge or resident service.\n\n## Checks\n\n- `cargo build`, `cargo fmt --check`, and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n- All 1,929 non-ignored Rust tests have passing observations across the full run and focused repairs; 12 ignored tests were not run.\n- Swift built; 278 tests exercised. Three stale chat-lens assertions were corrected from the source branch, then all 36 affected fixture/DTO/query tests passed. Multiplatform boundary check passed.\n- Affected Python tests: 70 passed initially; the remaining stale chat-vocabulary assertion was corrected and all four alignment tests passed.\n- Website CI exposed one stale daemon-security assertion; the source-branch correction passed its focused browser test.\n- Architecture coverage passed. Generated architecture HTML updated. Tests used an isolated Loopflow Home and database.\n\nReview caught obsolete daemon packaging, UI liveness claims and test CLI arguments; all were reconciled. An existing provider mock unexpectedly committed the staged file deletions under its fixture message; the following commit finishes the same reviewed cut. Squash landing retains this PR's title.","files":[],"additions":421,"deletions":35333,"changed_files":159,"merge_commit":"3dc89bc9a062148a884e36db8f9528842e833d13"},{"number":1361,"title":"Defer the hosted CI matrix until PR scratch is clear","body":"Checkpoint PRs previously ran the full hosted matrix and failed scratch cleanup while work was still in progress. This PR defers that matrix until scratch is clear, reducing checkpoint CI work while retaining full checks for landing candidates and the merge queue.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Run hosted CI only on landing candidates · LOO-343](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-343/run-hosted-ci-only-on-landing-candidates)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- PRs containing scratch artifacts report deferred proof and skip the matrix and `tests-result`. Scratch-free PRs run all checks, regardless of draft status.\n- Merge-queue and main runs still reject scratch artifacts. Missing scratch or failed classification still fails the aggregate; main retains existing proof reuse and cache warming.\n- Rust tests use `--no-fail-fast` to collect failures in one run.\n- Testing and delivery docs explain how existing scratch cleanup selects landing candidates.\n\nA skipped checkpoint is not passing proof. Enforcement before merge depends on the required merge queue rejecting scratch artifacts.\n\n## Checks\n\nRecorded validation passed: 35 focused Python tests, architecture coverage, website tests, Ruff, actionlint, and whitespace checks. ShellCheck was unavailable and disabled. Hosted checkpoint → candidate → merge-queue behavior remains unverified.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough, not yet performed on GitHub: publish a checkpoint with notes in `scratch/`. Its CI summary should report deferred proof, with matrix jobs skipped. Run `lf pr submit`; its existing cleanup should publish a scratch-free candidate and trigger the full matrix.","files":[],"additions":126,"deletions":34,"changed_files":4,"merge_commit":"4a696c074073ab78b3cc0963af89b75ed7192204"},{"number":1362,"title":"Bound agent launch context and keep progress out of Task steering","body":"Long Task threads and accumulated notes could overwhelm agent launches, while routine agent progress could return as new direction. This PR bounds launch input, preserves complete sources for targeted reading, and avoids replaying direction already delivered during a successful visit to the same Flow step.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Cap what each agent step re-reads · LOO-346](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-346/cap-what-each-agent-step-re-reads)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Budget Wave memory at 8,000 tokens, scratch notes collectively at 16,000, and launch messages at 16,000. Oversized sources become marked excerpts pointing to complete local snapshots.\n- Enforce a total launch limit of 64,000 cl100k tokens and 512 KiB, including structured-reply guidance. Oversized remaining input produces an actionable error before contacting the provider. IDE seeds and oversized live steering also use bounded messages.\n- Use existing Run evidence to acknowledge delivered direction separately for each structural step and invocation. Failed or interrupted attempts acknowledge nothing; undelivered late comments remain eligible.\n- Mark `lf task comment` publications inside a Run as progress and exclude them from steering. Agents can explicitly send direction with `--steer`; participant comments retain their existing behavior.\n- Record source reductions and original sizes in Run context evidence, and update agent guidance and documentation.\n\nHistorical unmarked comments remain eligible because their authorship cannot be inferred safely. The launch limit excludes provider-native instructions, tools, later file reads, and conversation history; complete overflow sources remain local to the checkout. Provider latency improvements remain unmeasured.\n\n## Checks\n\nRecorded affected-suite verification passed: architecture checks, formatting, all-target Clippy with warnings denied, 1,937 Rust tests, and 78 website tests; 12 Rust and three website tests were skipped. Production and test files are unchanged since that gate.\n\nSynthetic coverage includes a 384-comment launch with large memory and scratch sources, complete source preservation, explicit-input rejection, structured-reply overhead, successful-step acknowledgement, and oversized Unicode live steering. Full Python, Swift, app/UI, and standalone E2E suites were not run locally.","files":[],"additions":747,"deletions":25,"changed_files":22,"merge_commit":"da31960c790f400bd7e685b5f51479f52429193c"},{"number":1363,"title":"Prevent failed searches from falsely blocking Task handoff","body":"Failed searches could block Task handoff when their output included quoted permission-denial text from source files or archived JSON. This PR keeps those ordinary failures as tool output while preserving blockers for recognized execution-denial diagnostics.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Stop treating failed read-only commands as blocked capabilities · LOO-352](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-352/stop-treating-failed-read-only-commands-as-blocked-capabilities)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Require a failed command and a matching diagnostic line instead of searching aggregated output for denial substrings.\n- Report the matching diagnostic rather than unrelated trailing output.\n- Recognize connection refusals and missing executables alongside permission, filesystem, and network-policy denials.\n- Add focused regressions for both reported search patterns and a real macOS sandbox denial; document the handoff behavior.\n\nRecognition still relies on merged command output: arbitrary text reproducing a complete diagnostic can still trigger a blocker. Existing blocked Tasks are not automatically recovered.\n\n## Checks\n\nRecorded verification passed focused classifier and Task handoff tests, a real `sandbox-exec` denial, formatting, and all-target Clippy. Replays of both recorded incident outputs changed from blocked to unblocked; these were recorded observations, not live Task recovery.\n\nFresh gate formatting, diff, and architecture checks passed. The gate remains incomplete: free disk space was below the repository’s 32 GiB reserve, preventing the remaining behavioral, Clippy, and website checks from starting. Hosted CI and installed-binary behavior remain unverified.","files":[],"additions":107,"deletions":25,"changed_files":2,"merge_commit":"458fa141d2e6347c636441389d3896d941dcb839"},{"number":1364,"title":"Prioritize planned deletions before implementation and polishing","body":"Agents could spend time repairing code and fixtures that the plan already scheduled for removal. The builtin skills now explicitly put those deletions first, directing implementation and cleanup toward the code that will survive.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Make the deepest cuts first inside a Task · LOO-345](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-345/make-the-deepest-cuts-first-inside-a-task)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Design and kickoff plans identify concrete files, symbols, and exclusive tests or fixtures as **Delete — do not maintain**.\n- Implement and compress consume and update that list before building or polishing surviving code.\n- Required consumer cutovers, data migrations, and behavioral coverage stay in the same coherent change. Temporary breakage must be resolved before claiming proof; purely additive work requires no invented deletions.\n- Refresh the implement prompt golden to match the instructions.\n\n## Checks\n\nRecorded validation passed architecture checks, formatting, Clippy with warnings denied, and 1,932 tests, with 12 skipped. Compiled prompts for all four skills delivered the deletion marker and ordering.\n\nThese results cover the skill and golden content at `faa5b0777`; only the evidence note changed afterward. They establish prompt delivery and consistency, not measured reductions in agent churn or adoption by installed skills.","files":[],"additions":62,"deletions":21,"changed_files":5,"merge_commit":"e744f70690384f305755cadc638b8d14b6080d0e"},{"number":1365,"title":"Refresh account status and preserve account choices across Flow resumes","body":"Account status previously required an explicit refresh, and local account choices depended on the launching CLI staying alive. This PR makes managed status current by default and saves Claude and Codex selections through Flow recovery, while tightening identity checks and adding explicit banked reset redemption.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Keep account status live and choose accounts per Flow step · LOO-340](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-340/keep-account-status-live-and-choose-accounts-per-flow-step)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- `lf auth status` refreshes managed identity and usage. `--cached` preserves offline, read-only inspection; `--verify` is removed. Failed refreshes retain dated evidence, and expired usage displays as unknown.\n- Managed Codex authorization opens through the saved Chrome profile using app-server. Failed or canceled login preserves existing credentials.\n- Claude identity is bound to the credentials that were verified. Status and routing reject mismatched or duplicate identities; changed credentials require a fresh observation.\n- Flow and Task invocations capture per-provider `--account` or `--only-account` choices and restore them for autonomous steps, review children and resumes. Local selection survives CLI exit; SSH forwarding still requires its origin broker. Restart an invocation to change its saved choices.\n- Live Codex status shows available banked resets. Only `lf auth redeem-reset codex <email>` spends one, reporting before/after usage and an idempotency key for retrying a lost reply. A failed follow-up refresh preserves the confirmed redemption outcome.\n\nAccount state remains in the existing Home database; a forward migration adds the Claude credential binding.\n\n## Checks\n\nRecorded gate on September 30, after merging `main`: 1,945 Rust tests passed (12 skipped), and 78 website tests passed (3 skipped). Formatting, all-target Clippy, architecture coverage, migration history and skill-command alignment passed. The later commit changes only verification notes.\n\nAccount proofs used fake providers and disposable Homes, including mixed-provider Flow recovery and reset retries after a lost reply. Real browser OAuth and native Session resume remain unverified; no real reset was spent.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough, not performed against live accounts: run `lf auth status codex` with a managed login. It should show refreshed usage and any provider-reported reset credits. Then run `lf auth status codex --cached`; it should retain dated usage evidence, report reset credits as unknown and make no provider request.","files":[],"additions":1912,"deletions":585,"changed_files":31,"merge_commit":"e14a1d03518672794aa1615b9584cd54866ae20b"},{"number":1366,"title":"Keep saved plans from activating unrelated skills","body":"Historical skill mentions in saved plans and quoted notes could activate an unrelated skill during a later Run. This PR separates reference material from live requests so plans can carry decisions and evidence forward without reissuing old skill invocations.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Keep step-scoped framing out of persisted plans · LOO-350](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-350/keep-step-scoped-framing-out-of-persisted-plans)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Encode dollar signs as `&#36;` in submitted references, including scratch files, diffs, clipboard content, Wave memory, and recognized reference sections and blockquotes within messages. Direct skill requests remain active.\n- Label scratch content as reference material and warn with file paths and line numbers about session-specific instructions, Home claims, and dollar-prefixed mentions, including nested and untracked Markdown.\n- Teach plan-writing skills to preserve named, dated decisions, acceptance status, remaining work, and proof without carrying forward authoring-session instructions.\n- Preserve original files and gathered content while keeping the rendered references attributed in Run context.\n\nWarnings are advisory and can flag quoted examples; they neither block launch nor rewrite files.\n\n## Checks\n\nAdded regression coverage for implement launches containing historical kickoff mentions, direct skill requests, reference rendering, warning locations, and source attribution. Updated prompt goldens. Tests and lint were not run while preparing this description.","files":[],"additions":361,"deletions":58,"changed_files":14,"merge_commit":"31c6e5d8fb3ff4f339715e3f46acca116c406d9e"},{"number":1367,"title":"Merge Task branch updates without rewriting authored history","body":"Updating long Task branches could replay commits and repeatedly reopen conflicts. `lf sync` now merges main or the live stack parent into the branch, preserving authored commit IDs and resolved conflicts through synchronization and landing preparation.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Merge main into Task branches instead of rebasing · LOO-351](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-351/merge-main-into-task-branches-instead-of-rebasing)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Replace `lf rebase` with `lf sync`, with no CLI alias. Saved Flow commands migrate automatically while retaining their arguments and structure.\n- Preserve child edits after a parent lands by squash, using the recorded fork as the comparison base. Landing preparation retains branch history; GitHub performs the final squash onto main.\n- Start stacked children with a `Clear inherited scratch` commit and preserve their own notes and deletions during parent updates.\n- Allow agents to resolve unowned or stopped merges while retaining protection against a live foreign operation owner. Publish, submit, and landing recognize completed merges made outside Loopflow and reconcile the recorded Task base.\n\n## Checks\n\nRecorded local gate results for implementation commit `8ad76bc439`: 1,939 Rust tests passed, 294 Python tests passed, and 78 website tests passed. Formatting, all-target Clippy, architecture coverage, and changed-file Ruff checks passed. Earlier local verification passed all 13 shell safety scenarios.\n\nCoverage includes a 190-commit branch resolving one merge conflict without rewriting its commits, stacked children surviving parent squash landing, scratch preservation, and interrupted merge recovery. GitHub and provider interactions used local fixtures; hosted acceptance remains unverified. The final commit adds verification notes only; checks were not rerun for this draft.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough: on an authored Task branch behind main, run `lf sync --manual`. Resolve any conflicts and run `lf sync --continue`. Inspect `git log --graph --oneline`: the original commits should remain alongside the merge bringing in main. Repeat the sync without new upstream changes; the resolved conflict should stay resolved. Manual synchronization stays local and does not push.","files":[],"additions":1610,"deletions":1180,"changed_files":64,"merge_commit":"e88c34a674fed2f94b24964606fbcdfb91b760ec"}],"decisions":null,"previous_release_notes":"# v0.12.26\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.26 makes it easier to inspect what Loopflow will run and which managed login it will use. Local command, skill, and flow discovery explains available invocations before execution, while account identity checks catch mismatched logins before connecting or routing Codex work. Upgrade for clearer command selection and more reliable managed-account status, with two changes required for existing scripts and custom flows.\n\n## Find the invocation before starting work\n\nDiscovery now exposes command ownership and definition sources without launching agents, connecting accounts, or fetching definitions. Selection follows the same rules in CLI execution and flow composition.\n\n- Use `lf list`, `lf help NAME`, and `lf help --all` to find definitions, inspect their sources, and see usable invocations.\n- Unique shortcuts resolve to canonical commands: `lf land` selects `lf pr land`. Ambiguous names report the available canonical choices; commands retain precedence over definitions.\n- `lf run NAME` runs a definition. Untyped lookup prefers flows over same-named skills; `lf skill NAME` and `lf flow NAME` select only the requested kind. A malformed flow reports an error instead of silently falling back to a skill.\n- Saved execution retains captured instructions and the existing saved-plan encoding for resume.\n\n## Keep managed work on the intended login\n\nA configured email could previously appear verified while its credential belonged to another login. Managed-account checks now compare observed identity before connecting, accepting verified usage, or routing Codex work, and provide recovery commands when identities disagree.\n\n- Codex identity checks compare the reported email with its native credential and per-user identity. Claude connect/import and explicit verification use the provider profile’s email and UUID.\n- Duplicate managed logins and misleading email changes are rejected. Different people sharing a workspace remain valid, and staged reconnect keeps the installed credential while authorization waits.\n- Observed identity and plan persist without resetting configuration or cooldowns. Temporary verification outages preserve cached credential health; provider rejection marks credentials missing.\n- Automatic Codex routing prefers observed Pro plans over Plus among healthy candidates while preserving explicit preferences and Session pins.\n- `lf auth status codex` stays read-only and shows observed login and recovery guidance. Add `--verify` to request current identity and usage. Usage displays as used/left, and expired windows display as unknown.\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- **Script and flow migration:** replace `lf catalog` with `lf list`, and replace authored YAML `op:` steps with `cmd:`. Bundled flows are migrated. Review same-named skills and flows because untyped lookup now selects the flow.\n- **Account status scope:** state remains local to each Home. Ordinary status does not refresh provider observations; JSON retains dated usage observations, so consumers must check reset timestamps. Shared account state, current status by default, sole browser ownership, and Claude cached identity/routing remain follow-up work. Native provider credential writers do not participate in Loopflow’s installation lock.\n- **Validation limits:** account identity proofs use synthetic fixtures; live OAuth and deployed acceptance remain unverified. The supplied account-change record reports passing isolated Rust and website suites, formatting, Clippy, architecture, migration-history, and fresh-Home JSON checks. An earlier gate failed after inherited executable selection launched real Claude; that group was stopped and isolated checks subsequently passed. `TESTING.md` records the required isolation.\n- **Documentation previews:** proposed command-owner moves and overview commands are labeled designs, not shipped functionality.\n\n## Small changes\n\n- The new `pr-review` skill produces HTML code walkthroughs.\n- CLI documentation separates the workflow guide from the command reference.\n- External skills use consistent frontmatter parsing when fetched and when read from cache.","source_limits":{"context_bytes":131072,"commits":256,"merged_prs":200,"files_per_change":100,"area_scopes":32,"name_bytes":256,"title_bytes":300,"path_bytes":512,"pr_body_bytes":4096,"decisions_bytes":16384,"previous_release_notes_bytes":16384,"release_notes_bytes":61440},"omissions":{"commits":0,"merged_prs":0,"commit_files":59,"pr_files":0,"area_scopes":0,"text_bytes":0,"decisions_bytes":0,"previous_release_notes_bytes":0}}